00:40:18.180 --> 00:40:23.280
Last week, we announced a new
feature called API Security

00:40:23.280 --> 00:40:24.150
Reporting.

00:40:24.150 --> 00:40:26.100
And what this
feature essentially

00:40:26.100 --> 00:40:30.630
addresses is for the
security operations people,

00:40:30.630 --> 00:40:33.390
you can basically do
three different activities

00:40:33.390 --> 00:40:34.960
on this feature.

00:40:34.960 --> 00:40:41.640
One is you can very quickly
review which API proxies have

00:40:41.640 --> 00:40:44.250
been configured
with which policies

00:40:44.250 --> 00:40:46.260
across the entire organization.

00:40:46.260 --> 00:40:47.790
And this is across environments.

00:40:47.790 --> 00:40:51.420
This is across regions
and stuff like that.

00:40:51.420 --> 00:40:53.940
So if you as a sec
ops person would

00:40:53.940 --> 00:40:56.760
like to ensure that
all of your proxies

00:40:56.760 --> 00:40:59.730
have been configured,
for example, let's say

00:40:59.730 --> 00:41:02.940
[INAUDIBLE] policy, this is the
place where you can actually

00:41:02.940 --> 00:41:05.040
quickly verify and cross-check.

00:41:05.040 --> 00:41:08.310
And given the fact that
enterprises are now

00:41:08.310 --> 00:41:12.716
exposing business critical and
sensitive information to APIs,

00:41:12.716 --> 00:41:15.180
it is equally important
for the operations teams

00:41:15.180 --> 00:41:19.290
to also ensure that the right
people have the right access

00:41:19.290 --> 00:41:21.720
levels to the sensitive data.

00:41:21.720 --> 00:41:24.750
So data protection
is another capability

00:41:24.750 --> 00:41:26.190
within this feature,
where you can

00:41:26.190 --> 00:41:29.190
see who within your
organization is

00:41:29.190 --> 00:41:31.020
accessing the sensitive data.

00:41:31.020 --> 00:41:36.390
Has there been any anomaly in
terms of their access patterns?

00:41:36.390 --> 00:41:39.150
And if yes, then you can
quickly contact that person

00:41:39.150 --> 00:41:42.060
and understand why he or
she is actually trying

00:41:42.060 --> 00:41:45.240
to access the secure data.

00:41:45.240 --> 00:41:48.660
You can also view who
within your organization

00:41:48.660 --> 00:41:53.070
is exporting data out of the
platform to management APIs.

00:41:53.070 --> 00:41:54.940
By the way, I forgot
to mention that all

00:41:54.940 --> 00:41:59.200
of the capabilities
that you see in Apigee,

00:41:59.200 --> 00:42:02.520
including the analytics,
the custom reporting,

00:42:02.520 --> 00:42:04.560
